      "narrative": "Coker prescribes deriving the major triad by extracting scale degrees 1-3-5 from the major scale of the chord root: 'By extracting tones No. 1-3-5 from the C Major scale, we arrive at the notes forming the C Major Triad' (Chapter 1, p. 1). Students must be able to recite, write, and play major triads in every key before beginning pattern exercises (Chapter 1, p. 3).",
