      "chord_quality": "maj",
      "function_role": "tonic-major-bottom-structure-pattern-scope",
      "narrative": "Coker prescribes applying the 1-2-3-5 ascending pattern to any chord with a major third -- 'This pattern may be used on any chord with a major third' (Chapter 6, p. 25). This pattern, together with its minor counterpart 1-2-b3-5, is sufficient to cover virtually all chord changes in a standard tune: 'nearly all chords contained in the tune's progression will have either a major triad on the bottom (i.e., 1-2-3-5) or a minor triad' (Chapter 6, p. 29).",
