    {
      "chord_quality": "maj7",
      "function_role": "tonic-resolution-in-IIm7-V7-IM7",
      "narrative": "Coker prescribes treating the IM7 as the resolution target of the IIm7-V7-IM7 group and assigns it the major scale of its root for improvisation. The method extends one-measure IIm7-V7 patterns to accommodate the IM7 resolution by recycling mastered fragments rather than introducing new material: 'Rather than introducing new patterns, we will use four of the patterns previously discussed with the IIm7-V7 progression and extend them to the IM7' (Chapter 17, p. 90). All three chords share a single parent key signature (Chapter 16, p. 83).",
