      "chord_quality": "dom7",
      "function_role": "dominant-function-invariant-core",
      "narrative": "Coker prescribes a firm rule for dominant function: 'the chord retains its dominant function as long as the third is major and the seventh is minor, regardless of the type of ninth used' (Chapter 25, p. 119). This frees the improviser to alter the ninth, fifth, eleventh, and thirteenth freely. The fifth may be perfect, lowered, or raised; the eleventh perfect or augmented; the thirteenth major or (rarely) minor -- all without disturbing dominant function (Chapter 25, p. 121).",
