      "function_role": "dominant-shared-parent-key-with-IIm7",
      "narrative": "Coker prescribes exploiting the shared parent key of IIm7 and V7 to run a single scalar pattern across both chords without alteration: 'The pattern fits both chords because they both have the same parent key. Consequently, the accidentals in their respective scales are the same' (Chapter 17, p. 95). On a two-measure IIm7-V7, Coker assigns ascending direction to the IIm7 and descending direction to the V7: 'ascending the scale of the minor seventh chord and descending the scale of the dominant seventh chord' (Chapter 17, p. 94).",
