      "chord_quality": "dom7",
      "function_role": "dominant-diminished-half-step-color-tones",
      "narrative": "Coker prescribes using a diminished scale whose root sits one half-step above the dominant seventh chord root to simultaneously supply all four essential color tones: 'the root of the scale is a half-step above the root of the seventh chord (i.e, a C-sharp diminished scale is used with a C7)' (Chapter 27, p. 130). This yields flat-9, +9, +11, and 13 together -- 'all four color tones are common to one another and can be used together to good effect' (Chapter 27, p. 131).",
