      "chord_quality": "dom7",
      "function_role": "dominant-lydian-augmented-flat5-alignment",
      "narrative": "Coker prescribes one of two specific Lydian Augmented Scale alignments for dominant seventh flat-5 chords: 'In the case of the dominant 7th, flat 5th (b5), the root of the scale is the seventh of the chord' (Chapter 33, p. 146). This alignment yields an augmented eleventh (flat-5) color tone over the chord. Students must learn all twelve Lydian Augmented scales 'by playing them over and over throughout the range of your instrument' and in intervallic patterns such as thirds (Chapter 33, p. 146).",
