      "function_role": "dominant-lydian-augmented-altered-extensions-alignment",
      "narrative": "Coker prescribes a second Lydian Augmented Scale alignment for dominant chords with raised 5th, raised 9th, lowered 9th, and augmented 11th: 'In the case of the dominant 7th, raised 5th, raised 9th, lowered 9th, and augmented 11th, the root of the scale is the third of the chord' (Chapter 33, p. 146). This distinct root placement -- on the chord's third rather than its seventh -- simultaneously yields all four alterations, making it the prescribed scale source for this altered-dominant context.",
