      "function_role": "dominant-turnaround-endpoint",
      "narrative": "Coker prescribes that a turnaround (turnback) must end on a V7 chord or a flat-II7/flat-IIM7 dominant substitute: 'most will begin with a tonic chord (but only for about two beats) and will end with either a V7 chord (dominant) or a flat-II7 or flat-IM7 (dominant substitute)' (Chapter 25, p. 118). This gives phrase-endings 'a sense of direction, namely to return gracefully to the beginning of a repeated section' (Chapter 25, p. 118).",
