      "narrative": "Coker prescribes using the same Mixolydian scale for both dominant seventh and dominant ninth chords sharing the same root: 'Note that the same scale is used for dominant seventh and dominant ninth chords having the same root' (Chapter 9, p. 51). No separate scale or fingering is required; the ninth (scale degree 9 = scale degree 2) is already contained in the Mixolydian parent.",
