      "narrative": "Coker prescribes obtaining flat-9, +9, +11, and 13 simultaneously from the diminished scale positioned one half-step above the dominant seventh root: 'the pattern also yields the color tones of flat-9, +9, +11, and 13... the experienced improviser or arranger knows that all four color tones are common to one another and can be used together to good effect' (Chapter 27, p. 131). This is the book's primary prescription for fully altered dominant improvisation using a symmetrical scale source.",
