      "narrative": "Coker prescribes deriving the minor sixth chord by extracting scale degrees 1-3-5-6 from the Dorian mode: 'Tones No. 1-3-5-6 of the B Dorian Mode form the B Minor Sixth Chord' (Chapter 11, p. 62). All four minor chord types -- minor triad, m6, m7, m9 -- share the same Dorian mode parent and the same underlying triad: 'Note that all four chords contain the same triad, B, D, F-Sharp; and all four chords use the same basic scale, the B Dorian Mode, to establish their sound' (Chapter 12, p. 67).",
